7→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   208→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-24\",\n   209→    \"topics\": [\"LLM\", \"AI models\", \"DeepSeek\", \"cost-effective AI\"],\n   210→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   211→  },\n   212→  {\n   213→    \"title\": \"Honker: Postgres NOTIFY/LISTEN semantics for SQLite\",\n   214→    \"description\": \"A Rust SQLite extension implementing transactional outbox pattern with Kafka-style durable streams. Enables real-time queue processing with 1ms polling on .db-wal files.\",\n   215→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   216→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   217→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   218→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-24\",\n   219→    \"topics\": [\"SQLite\", \"databases\", \"queues\", \"Rust\", \"transactional-outbox\"],\n   220→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   221→  },\n   222→  {\n   223→    \"title\": \"Claude Code quality postmortem: Agentic systems have complex bugs\",\n   224→    \"description\": \"Anthropic released a postmortem on Claude Code quality issues. Three separate bugs in the Claude Code harness caused material problems, including a bug that made Claude seem forgetful by clearing thinking every turn instead of just once.\",\n   225→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   226→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   227→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   228→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-24\",\n   229→    \"topics\": [\"Claude Code\", \"Anthropic\", \"agentic systems\", \"debugging\", \"AI coding\"],\n   230→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   231→  },\n   232→  {\n   233→    \"title\": \"Bluesky's For You feed: 419GB SQLite on a gaming PC\",\n   234→    \"description\": \"The For You feed serving 72,000 Bluesky users runs on a single Go process with SQLite on a gaming PC (16 cores, 96GB RAM, 4TB NVMe). Stores 90 days of data. Total cost: $30/month. Architecture by spacecowboy.\",\n   235→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   236→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   237→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   238→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-24\",\n   239→    \"topics\": [\"Bluesky\", \"SQLite\", \"scaling\", \"Go\", \"architecture\"],\n   240→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   241→  },\n   242→  {\n   243→    \"title\": \"GPT-5.5 released with semi-official Codex backdoor API\",\n   244→    \"description\": \"OpenAI released GPT-5.5, available in OpenAI Codex and rolling out to paid ChatGPT subscribers. Early access shows it as fast, effective and highly capable.\",\n   245→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   246→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   247→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   248→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-23\",\n   249→    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"GPT-5.5\", \"LLM\", \"AI models\"],\n   250→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   251→  },\n   252→  {\n   253→    \"title\": \"Qwen3.6-27B: Flagship-level coding in 27B dense model\",\n   254→    \"description\": \"Qwen claims their new 27B model delivers flagship-level agentic coding performance, surpassing the previous 397B MoE model. The GGUF quantized version is 16.8GB. Tested with pelican bicycle SVG generation showing impressive results for local model.\",\n   255→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   256→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   257→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   258→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n   259→    \"topics\": [\"Qwen\", \"local LLMs\", \"coding models\", \"quantization\"],\n   260→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   261→  },\n   262→  {\n   263→    \"title\": \"Firefox 150: 271 vulnerabilities fixed by Claude Mythos Preview\",\n   264→    \"description\": \"Mozilla applied Claude Mythos Preview to Firefox, resulting in 271 vulnerability fixes in Firefox 150. Bobby Holley notes that defenders finally have a chance to win decisively against security issues.\",\n   265→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   266→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   267→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   268→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n   269→    \"topics\": [\"Firefox\", \"Claude\", \"security\", \"AI-assisted security\"],\n   270→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   271→  },\n   272→  {\n   273→    \"title\": \"GitHub Copilot pricing changes due to agentic workflows\",\n   274→    \"description\": \"GitHub changed Copilot Individual plans: tightening usage limits, pausing signups, restricting Claude Opus 4.7 to $39/month Pro+ plan. Agentic workflows fundamentally changed compute demands - long-running parallelized sessions consume far more resources.\",\n   275→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   276→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   277→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   278→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n   279→    \"topics\": [\"GitHub Copilot\", \"pricing\", \"agentic workflows\", \"LLM costs\"],\n   280→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   281→  },\n   282→  {\n   283→    \"title\": \"Claude Code pricing confusion around $100/month\",\n   284→    \"description\": \"Anthropic quietly updated pricing page then reverted it. The confusion around whether Claude Code would cost $100/month highlights uncertainty in AI coding tool pricing.\",\n   285→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   286→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   287→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   288→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n   289→    \"topics\": [\"Claude Code\", \"Anthropic\", \"pricing\", \"AI coding tools\"],\n   290→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   291→  },\n   292→  {\n   293→    \"title\": \"ChatGPT Images 2.0 released: GPT-3 to GPT-5 level leap\",\n   294→    \"description\": \"OpenAI released ChatGPT Images 2.0. Sam Altman said the leap from gpt-image-1 to gpt-image-2 was equivalent to jumping from GPT-3 to GPT-5.\",\n   295→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   296→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   297→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net\",\n   298→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n   299→    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"image generation\", \"GPT-5.5\", \"AI 